SUMMARY:U.S. IMMIGRATION PROGRAM IN CHALLENGING TIMES
LOCATION: Robert C. Byrd Center, Multipurpose Room (and Zoom)
DESCRIPTION:SPEAKER: Paul Grussendorf\n\n\n\n\nCOST: \n $15\; Free for Spring subscribers and SU students and employees\n \n \nPaul Grussendorf will provide a background to the U.S. asylum and refugee programs\, how they fit into American immigration law\, and how policies under the current administration have changed the landscape\, as well as present some ideas for comprehensive reform going forward.  \n \n \nAbout the Speaker: \nPaul Grussendorf was director of the Immigration Clinic at George Washington University for a decade. He served as an immigration judge in Philadelphia and San Francisco\, was a Refugee Officer with the US program from 2006 to 2011\, was a Supervisory Asylum Officer in the Arlington\, VA office from 2016 to 2019\, and is a consultant to the UN Refugee Agency. His book My Trials: Inside America’s Deportation Factories is a scathing indictment of America’s dysfunctional immigration system.\n \n 
